# Replica Integration for Cursor

## Overview
Replica provides fast, isolated workspaces for AI-assisted coding using APFS clonefile technology on macOS.

## When to Use Replica
- Starting a new coding task requiring a clean project state
- Running multiple Cursor sessions in parallel
- Need workspace creation in milliseconds (vs the seconds a git clone plus install takes)
- Disk space optimization via copy-on-write cloning

## Quick Start
```bash
# Create workspace and open in Cursor
cursor $(replica new --ttl 2h --name "my-task")

# Or from within Cursor terminal:
cd $(replica new --ttl 2h)
```

## Key Commands
- `replica new [--ttl 2h] [--name label]` - Create workspace
- `replica env <id>` - Get environment exports
- `replica list [--json]` - List workspaces
- `replica help [topic]` - Built-in guide
- `replica gc` - Clean up expired workspaces
- `replica stats` - Disk usage stats

## Configuration
```bash
export REPLICA_ROOT=/Volumes/Work/replica
```

## Workflow
1. `replica base build --repo <url> --setup "make deps"` (one-time)
2. `cd $(replica new)` - Instant workspace with deps ready
3. Code with Cursor
4. Workspace auto-expires or `replica rm <id>`

## Tips
- Shared caches in `$REPLICA_ROOT/cache` (cargo, npm, sccache)
- Call `replica touch <id>` from long sessions
- Use `--require-fresh` to ensure base is up-to-date

